fic information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le16ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Linking Words with the Same Consonant Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Linking words with the same consonant sounds smoothly connect one word to the next when speaking. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When a word ends in a consonant sound and the following word begins with the same consonant sound, we don't pronounce two sounds - both sounds are pronounced together as one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice pronouncing the linking words in the following examples."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":6,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"P-P\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"G-G\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"D-D\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"T-T\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"R-R\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"K-C\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" step parent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Big girl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" red dish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" get ten\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" wear red\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" dark color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ste<span class=\\\"strong\\\">p</span>arent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bi<span class=\\\"strong\\\">g</span>irl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"re<span class=\\\"strong\\\">d</span>ish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ge<span class=\\\"strong\\\">t</span>en\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wea<span class=\\\"strong\\\">r</span>ed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dar<span class=\\\"strong\\\">c</span>olor\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm a big girl, but for me, meeting someone in a club is unthinkable. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He wore big glasses, some make-up and dark coloured clothes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hi, do you speak Korean?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronunciating words with -able."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "One of the most common suffixes is -able. This changes a verb to an adjective."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you remove -able from a word, you are left with a complete word (breakable, break)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">-able is pronounced /\u0259bl/</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You stress the \u2018a' that comes right before \u2018ble'"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To think -     think-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble<br/>To believe -  believe-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say these words. Stress the bolded syllable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">replace-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;reli-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">believe-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;                           think-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">imagine-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;                         like-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "add the prefix -un:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"un-replace-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" un-reli-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"un-believe-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" un-imagine-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" un-think-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"un-like-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "-un does not change the stress it changes the meaning of the word."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My weekend was an unbelievable event. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had an unimaginable  Saturday evening."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Meeting someone in a club is unthinkable."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He was not unlikeable."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unbelievable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "too unlikely to be believed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My weekend was an unbelievable event."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you talk about attraction!"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unlikeable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not likely to be liked"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was not unlikeable - at all."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unthinkable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "impossible to conceive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Meeting someone in a club is unthinkable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to glance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look quickly or briefly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, when I was talking to my friend, you glanced over."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to melt"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to soften someone's feelings and emotions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I melted. It was magical. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "couldn't take my eyes off of someone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used when it is hard to stop looking at someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We talked some more, but I couldn't take my eyes off him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "love at first sight"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a feeling of warm personal attachment or deep affection "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As soon as I saw him I melted. I believe it was love at first sight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le16ob04aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Students brainstorm